 "blobs": {
  "sha256:50c83aef44b689b2b8eae978dad4725e35aa1944b7a5aab776f7ed3cad1cfebf": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 680\r\nWIRE -64 32 -64 16\r\nWIRE -64 16 16 16\r\nWIRE 96 16 208 16\r\nWIRE 160 16 160 -64\r\nWIRE 160 -64 304 -64\r\nWIRE 304 80 240 80\r\nWIRE 240 80 240 128\r\nWIRE -64 112 -64 128\r\nWIRE 416 48 480 48\r\nWIRE 384 -64 480 -64\r\nWIRE 480 -64 480 48\r\nWIRE 480 48 544 48\r\nWIRE 544 48 544 64\r\nWIRE 544 144 544 160\r\nFLAG 240 128 0\r\nFLAG -64 128 0\r\nFLAG 544 160 0\r\nFLAG 544 48 out\r\nFLAG 160 16 err\r\nSYMBOL voltage -64 16 M0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value AC 1\r\nSYMBOL res 112 0 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 400 -80 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R2\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 528 48 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL\r\nSYMATTR Value 2k\r\nSYMBOL Stability\\\\LoopProbe 256 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName LP1\r\nSYMBOL TCLib\\\\OA_param 496 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 -113 80 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 -176 32 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 123 -176 48 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 39 -176 64 Left 0\r\nSYMATTR InstName U1\r\nSYMATTR Value Av=1Meg\r\nSYMATTR Value2 f1=10\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine f2=1Meg\r\nTEXT -64 560 Left 2 ;LP1 (Stability > LoopProbe) is in series in the loop, at the error point: the loop signal goes from the summing node into the op amp (the arrow).\\nOutside .stb it is a plain wire. The .stb turns its sources on one at a time and computes T; next to the Bode plot: margins, poles and zeros of T,\\nclosed-loop poles and the root locus of 1 + k·T. U1 has two poles (10 Hz and 1 MHz): with gain -1 the phase margin is only about 25°.\r\nTEXT -64 664 Left 2 ;.stb LP1 dec 50 10 100meg\r\n",
  "sha256:45ea236bebd3b6f1a9eaf41e9171457999cfc0e3d12cfbc2778f644db869df92": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 680\r\nWIRE -64 32 -64 16\r\nWIRE -64 16 16 16\r\nWIRE 96 16 208 16\r\nWIRE 160 16 160 -64\r\nWIRE 160 -64 304 -64\r\nWIRE 304 80 240 80\r\nWIRE 240 80 240 128\r\nWIRE -64 112 -64 128\r\nWIRE 416 48 480 48\r\nWIRE 384 -64 480 -64\r\nWIRE 480 -64 480 48\r\nWIRE 480 48 544 48\r\nWIRE 544 48 544 64\r\nWIRE 544 144 544 160\r\nFLAG 240 128 0\r\nFLAG -64 128 0\r\nFLAG 544 160 0\r\nFLAG 544 48 out\r\nFLAG 160 16 err\r\nSYMBOL voltage -64 16 M0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value AC 1\r\nSYMBOL res 112 0 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 400 -80 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R2\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 528 48 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL\r\nSYMATTR Value 2k\r\nSYMBOL Stability\\\\LoopProbe 256 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName LP1\r\nSYMBOL TCLib\\\\OA_param 496 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 -113 80 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 -176 32 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 123 -176 48 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 39 -176 64 Left 0\r\nSYMATTR InstName U1\r\nSYMATTR Value Av=1Meg\r\nSYMATTR Value2 f1=10\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine f2=1Meg\r\nTEXT -64 560 Left 2 ;Middlebrook's GFT with input V1 and output V(out): it gives the asymptotic gain model G = G∞·R/(1+R) + G0/(1+R):\\nG (closed loop), G∞ (ideal, -R2/R1 = -1), G0 (direct path) and R (return ratio). The probe must be at the error point and the signal must enter by its arrow; check G∞ first.\r\nTEXT -64 640 Left 2 ;.stb LP1 dec 50 10 100meg gft V1 V(out)\r\n",
  "sha256:d697ba9d2568500f791bfd4729320cbd470ecf8e213364e7e4e39be0a598dc73": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 680\r\nWIRE -64 32 -64 16\r\nWIRE -64 16 16 16\r\nWIRE 96 16 208 16\r\nWIRE 160 16 160 -64\r\nWIRE 160 -64 304 -64\r\nWIRE 304 80 240 80\r\nWIRE 240 80 240 128\r\nWIRE -64 112 -64 128\r\nWIRE 416 48 480 48\r\nWIRE 384 -64 480 -64\r\nWIRE 480 -64 480 48\r\nWIRE 480 48 544 48\r\nWIRE 544 48 544 64\r\nWIRE 544 144 544 160\r\nFLAG 240 128 0\r\nFLAG -64 128 0\r\nFLAG 544 160 0\r\nFLAG 544 48 out\r\nFLAG 160 16 err\r\nSYMBOL voltage -64 16 M0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value AC 1\r\nSYMBOL res 112 0 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 400 -80 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R2\r\nSYMATTR Value 10k\r\nSYMBOL res 528 48 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL\r\nSYMATTR Value 2k\r\nSYMBOL Stability\\\\LoopProbe 256 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName LP1\r\nSYMBOL TCLib\\\\OA_param 496 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 -113 80 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 -176 32 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 123 -176 48 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 39 -176 64 Left 0\r\nSYMATTR InstName U1\r\nSYMATTR Value Av=1Meg\r\nSYMATTR Value2 f1=10\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine f2=1Meg\r\nTEXT -64 560 Left 2 ;With R2 = 10k the feedback factor drops to 1/11: T crosses 0 dB lower, far from the 1 MHz pole, and the margin rises to about 54°.\r\nTEXT -64 616 Left 2 ;.stb LP1 dec 50 10 100meg\r\n",
  "sha256:e832cb5421b2e08922febd547739e64c29ae8393437bff05b13208363da23a93": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 680\r\nWIRE -64 32 -64 16\r\nWIRE -64 16 16 16\r\nWIRE 96 16 208 16\r\nWIRE 160 16 160 -64\r\nWIRE 160 -64 304 -64\r\nWIRE 304 80 240 80\r\nWIRE 240 80 240 128\r\nWIRE -64 112 -64 128\r\nWIRE 416 48 480 48\r\nWIRE 384 -64 480 -64\r\nWIRE 480 -64 480 48\r\nWIRE 480 48 544 48\r\nWIRE 544 48 544 64\r\nWIRE 544 144 544 160\r\nFLAG 240 128 0\r\nFLAG -64 128 0\r\nFLAG 544 160 0\r\nFLAG 544 48 out\r\nFLAG 160 16 err\r\nSYMBOL voltage -64 16 M0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Invisible 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value PULSE(0 0.1 0 10n 10n 5u 10u) AC 1\r\nSYMBOL res 112 0 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 400 -80 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R2\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 528 48 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL\r\nSYMATTR Value 2k\r\nSYMBOL Stability\\\\LoopProbe 256 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName LP1\r\nSYMBOL TCLib\\\\OA_param 496 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 -113 80 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 -176 32 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 123 -176 48 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 39 -176 64 Left 0\r\nSYMATTR InstName U1\r\nSYMATTR Value Av=1Meg\r\nSYMATTR Value2 f1=10\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine f2=1Meg\r\nTEXT -64 560 Left 2 ;The ringing of the step response is the 25° phase margin. The probe does not change the circuit: this is the same as without it.\r\nTEXT -64 616 Left 2 !.tran 20u\r\n",
  "sha256:f10829117a6259560dc180a98e93eba173dfea7620351cb3e3aa25580e7cb02b": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1200 680\r\nWIRE -64 32 -64 16\r\nWIRE -64 16 16 16\r\nWIRE 96 16 208 16\r\nWIRE 160 16 160 -64\r\nWIRE 160 -64 304 -64\r\nWIRE 304 80 240 80\r\nWIRE 240 80 240 128\r\nWIRE -64 112 -64 128\r\nWIRE 416 48 480 48\r\nWIRE 384 -64 480 -64\r\nWIRE 480 -64 480 48\r\nWIRE 480 48 544 48\r\nWIRE 544 48 544 64\r\nWIRE 544 144 544 160\r\nFLAG 240 128 0\r\nFLAG -64 128 0\r\nFLAG 544 160 0\r\nFLAG 544 48 out\r\nFLAG 160 16 err\r\nSYMBOL voltage -64 16 M0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName V1\r\nSYMATTR Value AC 1\r\nSYMBOL res 112 0 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 400 -80 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R2\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 528 48 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL\r\nSYMATTR Value 2k\r\nSYMBOL Stability\\\\LoopProbe 256 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName LP1\r\nSYMBOL TCLib\\\\OA_param 496 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 -113 80 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 -176 32 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 123 -176 48 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 39 -176 64 Left 0\r\nSYMATTR InstName U1\r\nSYMATTR Value Av=1Meg\r\nSYMATTR Value2 f1=10\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine f2=1Meg\r\nTEXT -64 224 Left 2 !.ac dec 50 10 100meg\r\n",
  "sha256:4c6178cd562807bdb330ade1711f3a8b80d081bc205c6980f8d53026096e56c6": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1400 900\r\nWIRE -64 32 -64 16\r\nWIRE -64 16 16 16\r\nWIRE 96 16 208 16\r\nWIRE 160 16 160 -64\r\nWIRE 160 -64 304 -64\r\nWIRE 384 -64 560 -64\r\nWIRE 560 -64 560 48\r\nWIRE 560 48 624 48\r\nWIRE -64 112 -64 128\r\nWIRE 208 16 304 16\r\nWIRE 304 80 272 80\r\nWIRE 416 48 464 48\r\nWIRE -64 352 -64 336\r\nWIRE -64 336 16 336\r\nWIRE 96 336 208 336\r\nWIRE 160 336 160 256\r\nWIRE 160 256 304 256\r\nWIRE 384 256 560 256\r\nWIRE 560 256 560 368\r\nWIRE 560 368 624 368\r\nWIRE -64 432 -64 448\r\nWIRE 208 336 304 336\r\nWIRE 304 400 272 400\r\nWIRE 416 368 464 368\r\nWIRE 832 160 784 160\r\nWIRE 832 224 784 224\r\nWIRE 928 160 976 160\r\nWIRE 928 224 976 224\r\nWIRE 880 448 976 448\r\nWIRE 928 448 928 496\r\nWIRE 928 496 928 496\r\nWIRE 928 544 928 576\r\nWIRE 976 560 976 576\r\nWIRE 976 480 1040 480\r\nFLAG -64 128 0\r\nFLAG 272 80 vcmfb\r\nFLAG 464 48 op\r\nFLAG 624 48 outp\r\nFLAG 560 48 outp\r\nFLAG -64 448 0\r\nFLAG 272 400 vcmfb\r\nFLAG 464 368 on\r\nFLAG 624 368 outn\r\nFLAG 560 368 outn\r\nFLAG 784 160 op\r\nFLAG 784 224 on\r\nFLAG 976 160 outp\r\nFLAG 976 224 outn\r\nFLAG 800 448 outp\r\nFLAG 1056 448 outn\r\nFLAG 928 448 cm\r\nFLAG 928 576 0\r\nFLAG 976 576 0\r\nFLAG 1040 480 vcmfb\r\nSYMBOL voltage -64 16 M0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Vp\r\nSYMATTR Value AC 0.5\r\nSYMBOL res 112 0 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1p\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 400 -80 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R2p\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL TCLib\\\\OA_param 496 0 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 -113 80 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 -176 32 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 123 -176 48 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 39 -176 64 Left 0\r\nSYMATTR InstName Up\r\nSYMATTR Value Av=1Meg\r\nSYMATTR Value2 f1=10\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine f2=1Meg\r\nSYMBOL voltage -64 336 M0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Vn\r\nSYMATTR Value AC 0.5 180\r\nSYMBOL res 112 320 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R1n\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 400 240 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName R2n\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL TCLib\\\\OA_param 496 320 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 -113 80 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 -176 32 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 123 -176 48 Left 0\r\nWINDOW 39 -176 64 Left 0\r\nSYMATTR InstName Un\r\nSYMATTR Value Av=1Meg\r\nSYMATTR Value2 f1=10\r\nSYMATTR SpiceLine f2=1Meg\r\nSYMBOL Stability\\\\DiffLoopProbe 880 192 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName LP1\r\nSYMBOL res 896 432 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Rcp\r\nSYMATTR Value 10k\r\nSYMBOL res 1072 432 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Rcn\r\nSYMATTR Value 10k\r\nSYMBOL e 976 464 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName Ecmfb\r\nSYMATTR Value -1\r\nTEXT -64 560 Left 2 ;LP1 (Stability > DiffLoopProbe) is in series in the differential output, between the op amp outputs (op, on) and the outputs (outp, outn).\\nInside, two ideal baluns back to back (E + F pairs: they neither isolate nor load) separate the differential and common modes,\\nwith a probe in each mode; the .stb chooses one (dm or cm). In DM the loop is the R2/R1 network of each half: the same T as the single-ended one.\r\nTEXT -64 664 Left 2 ;.stb LP1 dm dec 50 10 100meg\r\n",
